Found by a coordinator feature-gap review, 2026-08-30. Depends on B035
(code-action seam, kinds, resolve, fixAll).

## Gap
Three diagnostic families already KNOW their own fix and write it into the
message text, then offer no edit. The analysis is done; only the edit is
missing. These are the cheapest quick fixes in the codebase.

### 1. `StringByValueParam` (src/typecheck/checker.rs)
Message: "Sanity check: Use 'const string &in {}' to pass a string by
reference". The replacement string is literally in the diagnostic.
Fix: replace the parameter's type span `string` -> `const string &in`.

### 2. `RemovedApiUsage { member, hint }` (src/typecheck/checker.rs:~37)
The STRUCT CARRIES the replacement in `hint` (GH #27/#28 family, e.g.
`awaitable.WithRunContext`). Compiles clean today, deprecated no-op at
runtime.
Fix: replace the member span with the hint's replacement. The hint is prose
today, so this needs a structured replacement field OR a parse of the hint —
prefer adding a structured `replacement: Option<String>` to the variant and
keeping `hint` as the human sentence.

### 3. Unused declarations (B030 family)
Message ends "(prefix the parameter name with an underscore to ignore this
warning)". Fix text, again, already in the message.
Fixes: (a) prefix the name with `_`; (b) remove the declaration entirely where
it is a local or an unused import-like declaration. Offer both; neither is
`isPreferred` for locals (removal is lossy), but `_` prefixing IS preferred
for parameters, where removal would change the signature.

## Work
- Add a structured `replacement` to `RemovedApiUsage` rather than re-parsing
  the prose hint. Prose is for humans; the edit needs data.
- Implement the three producers against the B035 registry.
- All three are pure span replacements — no symbol-table lookups, no
  cross-file edits. Keep them that way; that is why this batch is first.

## Test plan (TDD, red first)
Red, one per family: a fixture with the diagnostic -> a `quickfix` action is
offered whose applied edit yields the expected text.

Variants (per CLAUDE.md, generalize):

`StringByValueParam`, over the full parameter-shape matrix:
- `string s` -> `const string &in s`
- already-correct forms offered NO fix: `const string &in s`, `string &in s`,
  `string &out s`, `string &inout s`, `string@ s`, `const string@ s`,
  `string@ &in s`
- underscore-prefixed `string _s` (currently suppressed) -> no fix offered
- multiple string params in one signature -> one fix each, all applicable
  together via fixAll without corrupting offsets
- a `string` param with a DEFAULT value (`string s = "x"`) -> type span only,
  default untouched
- a `string` param in a METHOD, a namespaced function, a funcdef, and a
  lambda/anonymous context if the grammar has one
- `array<string>` and `dictionary` params -> NOT matched (guard against a
  naive substring match on "string")
- a param literally named `string` (shadowing) -> no false rewrite

`RemovedApiUsage`:
- hint with a direct replacement -> applied
- hint with NO mechanical replacement -> diagnostic still published, NO action
  offered (must not offer a fix it cannot make)
- member appearing twice on one line -> only the diagnosed span is edited

Unused:
- parameter -> `_` prefix preferred; removal NOT offered (signature change)
- local variable -> both offered, neither preferred
- name already starting with `_` -> no action (guard against `__x`)
- removal of a local whose initializer has SIDE EFFECTS -> removal must not be
  offered, or must be marked non-preferred with the initializer retained;
  decide and document which, this is the one genuinely lossy case in the batch

## Related
B035 (seam), B037, B038. Fixture baselines must not move — these actions add
no diagnostics.